@startuml AuthenticationActivityStandard
!theme plain
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam BoxPadding 20

title User Registration & Login Activity

start
:User opens frontend application;
:Navigate to authentication page;

if (User action?) then (Register)
  :Click "Register" button;
  :Fill registration form;
  
  if (Form validation passes?) then (yes)
    :Submit registration data to API Gateway;
    :API Gateway validates email format;
    :Check password strength requirements;
    
    if (Email already exists in database?) then (yes)
      :API Gateway returns 409 Conflict;
      :Frontend shows "Email already registered" error;
      :User enters different email;
    else (no)
      :API Gateway creates user account in PostgreSQL;
      :Generate JWT access and refresh tokens;
      :Store refresh token in database;
      :API Gateway returns user data + tokens;
      :Frontend stores tokens in localStorage;
      :Show "Registration successful" message;
      :Redirect to main dashboard;
    endif
    
  else (no)
    :Show validation errors (email format, password strength);
    :User corrects form fields;
  endif
  
elseif (Login with Email/Password) then (Login)
  :Enter email and password;
  :Click "Login" button;
  
  if (Form validation passes?) then (yes)
    :Send credentials to API Gateway;
    :API Gateway extracts client info (IP, User-Agent);
    :Validate credentials against PostgreSQL database;
    
    if (Credentials are valid?) then (yes)
      :Generate JWT access and refresh tokens;
      :Store refresh token with expiration;
      :API Gateway returns tokens + user info;
      :Frontend stores tokens in localStorage;
      :Update user authentication state;
      :Redirect to main application;
    else (no)
      :API Gateway returns 401 Unauthorized;
      :Frontend shows "Invalid email or password" error;
      :User can retry login attempt;
    endif
    
  else (no)
    :Show validation errors;
    :User corrects input fields;
  endif
  
elseif (Login with Google OAuth) then (Google Login)
  :Click "Login with Google" button;
  :Redirect to Google OAuth consent screen;
  :User grants permission to application;
  :Google returns authorization code;
  :Frontend sends code to API Gateway;
  
  if (Google token validation succeeds?) then (yes)
    :Extract user profile from Google;
    :Find existing user or create new account;
    :Generate JWT access and refresh tokens;
    :Store Google credentials + refresh token;
    :API Gateway returns tokens + user info;
    :Frontend stores tokens and updates state;
    :Show successful login message;
  else (no)
    :API Gateway returns OAuth validation error;
    :Frontend shows "Google login failed" message;
    :User can retry with different Google account;
  endif
endif

:User is now authenticated and can access application;

if (Access token expires?) then (yes)
  :Frontend sends refresh token to API Gateway;
  :API Gateway validates refresh token in database;
  
  if (Refresh token valid and not expired?) then (yes)
    :Generate new access token;
    :Update refresh token expiration;
    :API Gateway returns new access token;
    :Frontend updates stored token;
  else (no)
    :API Gateway returns 401 Unauthorized;
    :Frontend clears all tokens;
    :Redirect user to login page;
  endif
endif

if (User wants to logout?) then (yes)
  :User clicks "Logout" button;
  :Frontend sends refresh token to API Gateway;
  :API Gateway validates JWT from Authorization header;
  :Delete refresh token from database;
  :Record logout timestamp for security audit;
  :API Gateway confirms logout success;
  :Frontend clears localStorage tokens;
  :Update UI to logged-out state;
  :Redirect to login page;
endif

if (Admin needs to revoke user token?) then (yes)
  :Admin sends revoke request to API Gateway;
  :API Gateway validates admin JWT and permissions;
  :Delete specified refresh token from database;
  :Record revocation timestamp and admin ID;
  :API Gateway confirms revocation success;
  :Admin receives confirmation message;
endif

if (External service needs authentication?) then (yes)
  :External service sends request to /auth/forward-auth;
  :API Gateway extracts user from JWT in request.state;
  :Validate user exists and is active in database;
  
  if (User valid and has required permissions?) then (yes)
    :Set response headers (X-User-ID, X-User-Email, X-User-Roles);
    :Return 200 OK with user context;
    :External service can proceed with request;
  else (no)
    :Return 401/403 Forbidden;
    :External service denies access;
  endif
endif

stop

note right
  **Security Features:**
  - JWT-based stateless authentication
  - Refresh token rotation for security
  - Rate limiting on authentication endpoints
  - Forward-auth pattern for microservices
  - Google OAuth2 integration
  - Role-based access control (RBAC)
  - Audit logging for security events
  - Protection against brute force attacks
end note

@enduml
